---
import PageWithSideBarNav from "@/layouts/PageWithSideBarNav.astro";
import Accordian from "../components/Accordian.astro";
import RootLayout from "../layouts/RootLayout.astro";
const pageTitle = "Hotlines and Assistance Centers";

// TODO: get posts for each category on this page
---

<RootLayout pageTitle={pageTitle}>
  <PageWithSideBarNav>
    <h1>{pageTitle}</h1>
    <div class="usa-prose">
      <p>
        The Hotlines and Assistance Centers page provides information, links,
        and phone numbers to various Federally-funded and non-profit
        environmental hotlines and compliance assistance centers.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="usa-accordion">
      <h4 class="usa-accordion__heading">
        <button
          type="button"
          class="usa-accordion__button"
          aria-expanded="false"
          aria-controls={"EnvironmentalHotlines"}
        >
          <h3>Environmental Hotlines</h3>
        </button>
      </h4>
      <div
        id={"EnvironmentalHotlines"}
        class="usa-accordion__content border radius-md border-base-lighter"
      >
        <ul class="usa-list">
          <li>
            <a
              href="https://www.epa.gov/aboutepa/epa-hotlines"
              class="usa-link usa-link--external">EPA Hotlines</a
            >
            <p class="margin-top-0">
              A list of hotlines and service lines for specific topics.
            </p>
          </li>
          <hr />
          <li>
            <a
              href="https://www.epa.gov/amtic/forms/contact-us-about-ambient-monitoring-technology-information-center-amtic"
              class="usa-link usa-link--external"
              >Ambient Monitoring Technology Information Center</a
            >
            <p class="margin-top-0">
              The Ambient Monitoring Technology Information Center (AMTIC) is
              operated by EPA's Monitoring and Quality Assurance Group (MQAG).
              AMTIC Contains information and files on ambient air quality
              monitoring programs, details on monitoring methods, relevant
              documents and articles, information on air quality trends and
              nonattainment areas, and federal regulations related to ambient
              air quality monitoring.
            </p>
          </li>
          <hr />
          <li>
            <a
              href="https://www.epa.gov/asbestos/forms/contact-us-about-asbestos"
              class="usa-link usa-link--external"
              >Asbestos Abatement/Management Ombudsman, 1-800-368-5888</a
            >
            <p class="margin-top-0">
              Provides public information on handling, abatement and management
              of asbestos. The hours of operation are 8:00 am to 3:30 pm.
            </p>
          </li>
          <hr />
          <li>
            <a
              href="https://www.epa.gov/catc"
              class="usa-link usa-link--external"
              >Clean Air Technology Center (CATC), Infoline 919-541-0800
              (English), 919-541-1800 (Spanish), (919) 541-5450 (fax)</a
            >
            <p class="margin-top-0">
              The Clean Air Technology Center (CATC) serves as a resource on all
              areas of emerging and existing air pollution prevention and
              control technologies, and provides public access to data and
              information on their use, effectiveness and cost. In addition, the
              CATC will provide technical support, including access to EPA?'s
              knowledge base, to government agencies and others, as resources
              allow, related to the technical and economic feasibility,
              operation and maintenance of these technologies.
            </p>
          </li>
          <hr />
          <li>
            <a
              href="https://www.epa.gov/chief"
              class="usa-link usa-link--external"
              >Clearinghouse for Inventories and Emission Factors (CHIEF),
              info_chief@epa.gov</a
            >
            <p class="margin-top-0">
              The clearinghouse provides information on air emissions modeling,
              electronic reporting of air emissions, emission factors estimation
              tools, and basic information about monitoring techniques.
            </p>
          </li>
          <hr />
          <li>
            <a
              href="https://www.epa.gov/emc"
              class="usa-link usa-link--external"
              >Emissions Measurement Center (EMC), Staff Directory</a
            >
            <p class="margin-top-0">
              EMC provides information on test methods for measuring pollutants
              from smokestacks and other industrial sources. This website
              compiles the test methods available for emission measurement.
            </p>
          </li>
          <hr />
          <li>
            <a
              href="http://www.epa.gov/compliance/assistance/index.html"
              class="usa-link usa-link--external"
              >EPA's National Compliance Assistance</a
            >
            <p class="margin-top-0">
              Compliance assistance providers help regulated communities and
              businesses comply with environmental laws through one-to-one
              counseling, online resource centers, fact sheets, guides and
              training. Providers include EPA regional office staff; state,
              local and tribal governments; federal and state small business and
              pollution prevention technical assistance extension agents,
              consultants, and trade associations.
            </p>
          </li>
          <hr />
          <li>
            <a
              href="https://www.epa.gov/lead/forms/lead-hotline-national-lead-information-center"
              class="usa-link usa-link--external"
              >Lead Hotline - National Lead Information Center (NLIC),
              1-800-424-LEAD, (1-800-424-5323)</a
            >
            <p class="margin-top-0">
              This hotline provides the general public and professionals with
              information about lead, lead hazards, and their prevention. The
              NLIC operates under a contract with the U.S. Environmental
              Protection Agency (EPA), with funding from EPA and the Department
              of Housing and Urban Development (HUD).
            </p>
          </li>
          <hr />
          <li>
            <a
              href="http://npic.orst.edu/index.html"
              class="usa-link usa-link--external"
              >National Pesticide Information Center, 1-800-858-7378, email:
              npic@ace.orst.edu</a
            >
            <p class="margin-top-0">
              This hotline offers science-based information about a wide variety
              of pesticide-related subjects and serves as a source of factual
              chemical, health, and environmental information about more than
              600 pesticide active ingredients incorporated into over 50,000
              different products registered for use in the United States since
              1947.
            </p>
          </li>
          <hr />
          <li>
            <a
              href="https://www.fedcenter.gov/_plugins/programs/remotelink/rlnk.cfm?dest=https://sosradon.org/national-radon-hotlines"
              class="usa-link usa-link--external"
              >National Radon Hotlines, 1-800-767-7236, email: Radon@ksu.edu</a
            >
            <p class="margin-top-0">
              Provides answers to questions regarding radon.
            </p>
          </li>
          <hr />
          <li>
            <a href="https://nrc.uscg.mil/" class="usa-link usa-link--external"
              >National Response Center Hotline, 1-800-424-8802</a
            >
            <p class="margin-top-0">Use to report spills.</p>
          </li>
          <hr />
          <li>
            <a
              href="https://www.epa.gov/nscep"
              class="usa-link usa-link--external"
              >National Service Center for Environmental Publications (NSCEP),
              email: nscep_nepis.tech@epa.gov</a
            >
            <p class="margin-top-0">
              The National Service Center for Environmental Publications
              maintains and distributes EPA publications in hardcopy, CD ROM and
              other multimedia formats. The publication inventory includes over
              7,000 titles, NSCEP also develops and distributes the annual EPA
              National Publications Catalog.
            </p>
          </li>
          <hr />
          <li>
            <a
              href="https://actat.wvu.edu/about-actat/national-small-flows-clearinghouse"
              class="usa-link usa-link--external"
              >National Small Flows Clearinghouse Hotline, email:
              info@mail.nesc.wvu.edu</a
            >
            <p class="margin-top-0">
              The National Small Flows Clearinghouse (NSFC) was funded by the
              U.S. Environmental Protection Agency to help America's small
              communities and individuals solve their wastewater problems
              through objective information about onsite wastewater collection
              and treatment systems.
            </p>
          </li>
          <hr />
          <li>
            <a
              href="https://www.epa.gov/p2/pollution-prevention-resources#ppic"
              class="usa-link usa-link--external"
              >Pollution Prevention Information Clearinghouse, 202-566-0799,
              p2hub@epa.gov</a
            >
            <p class="margin-top-0">
              Dedicated to reducing or eliminating industrial pollutants through
              technology transfer.
            </p>
          </li>
          <hr />
          <li>
            <a
              href="https://cfpub.epa.gov/RBLC/"
              class="usa-link usa-link--external"
              >Reasonably Available Control Technology (RACT)/ Best Available
              Control Technology (BACT)/ Lowest Achievable Emission Rate (LAER)
              Clearinghouse (RBLC), 919-541-4991 (fax)</a
            >
            <p class="margin-top-0">
              The RBLC provides information on the application of pollution
              prevention and control technologies to stationary air pollution
              sources through the OAQPS Technology Transfer Network (TTN)
              Bulletin Board System (BBS). The RBLC offers an on-line database
              with menu based searching, downloading of user-selected
              information, complete data viewing capabilities, context sensitive
              help functions, and data entry capabilities. It also offers a
              brochure, an informational flyer, the RBLC User's Manual (EPA-
              456/B-98-002), and annual reports documenting additions and
              changes to the system.
            </p>
          </li>
          <hr />
          <li>
            <a
              href="https://www.epa.gov/ground-water-and-drinking-water/safe-drinking-water-hotline"
              class="usa-link usa-link--external"
              >Safe Drinking Water Hotline, PFAS Inquiries: pfasnpdwr@epa.gov;
              Lead and Copper Rule Improvements: LCRI@epa.gov</a
            >
            <p class="margin-top-0">
              Provides information about EPA's drinking water regulations and
              other related drinking water and ground water topics to the
              regulated community, State and local officials.
            </p>
          </li>
          <hr />
          <li>
            <a
              href="http://www.epa.gov/tri/"
              class="usa-link usa-link--external"
              >Toxic Release Inventory - Community Right To Know - EPCRA
              Hotline, General Inquiries: tri.help@epa.gov; Other Program
              Contacts</a
            >
            <p class="margin-top-0">
              The Toxics Release Inventory (TRI) is a source of information
              concerning waste management activities and toxic chemicals that
              are being used, manufactured, treated, transported, or released
              into the environment. Two statutes, Section 313 of the Emergency
              Planning and Community Right-To-Know Act (EPCRA) and section 6607
              of the Pollution Prevention Act (PPA), mandate that a publicly
              accessible toxic chemical database be developed and maintained by
              US EPA.
            </p>
          </li>
          <hr />
          <li>
            <a
              href="https://www.epa.gov/aboutepa/epa-hotlines#toxic-substances-control-act-tsca-hotline"
              class="usa-link usa-link--external"
              >Toxic Substances Control Act (TSCA) Hotline, 202-554-1404,
              202-554-5603 (fax), email: tsca-hotline@epa.gov</a
            >
            <p class="margin-top-0">
              TSCA Hotline provides general information on requirements under
              the Toxic Substances Control Act (TSCA).
            </p>
          </li>
          <hr />
          <li>
            <a
              href="http://www.tercenter.org/"
              class="usa-link usa-link--external"
              >Transportation Environmental Resource Center (TERC)</a
            >
            <p class="margin-top-0">
              The Transportation Environmental Resource Center (TERC) provides
              environmental compliance information through the web-site and a
              toll free fax-back. The information is especially useful for
              airports and airlines, railroads, barging, ports and motor carrier
              industries. The goal of the TERC center is to identify up-to-date
              information on environmental compliance requirements and to make
              that information available to transportation professionals and the
              public. The American Association of Airport Executives (AAAE)
              manages the TERC, with the trucking page managed by the American
              Trucking Associations.
            </p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="usa-accordion">
      <h4 class="usa-accordion__heading">
        <button
          type="button"
          class="usa-accordion__button"
          aria-expanded="false"
          aria-controls={"ComplianceAssistanceCenters"}
        >
          <h3>Compliance Assistance Centers</h3>
        </button>
      </h4>
      <div
        id={"ComplianceAssistanceCenters"}
        class="usa-accordion__content border radius-md border-base-lighter"
      >
        <li>
          <a
            href="http://www.cicacenter.org/"
            class="usa-link usa-link--external"
            >Bookmark Construction Industry Compliance Assistance Center (CICA)</a
          >
          <p class="margin-top-0">
            CICA is your source for plain language explanations of environmental
            rules for the construction industry. The information is provided by
            the National Center for Manufacturing Sciences with the assistance
            of the Associated General Contractors of America and the National
            Association of Home Builders, in cooperation with the U.S.
            Environmental Protection Agency.
          </p>
        </li>
        <hr />
        <li>
          <a
            href="http://www.ecarcenter.org/"
            class="usa-link usa-link--external"
            >Bookmark Environmental Compliance for Automotive Recyclers (ECAR)</a
          >
          <p class="margin-top-0">
            This is a website designed by and for people in the automotive
            recycling business. The site includes a state-by-state analysis of
            applicable regulatory requirements for automotive recycling.
          </p>
        </li>
        <hr />
        <li>
          <a
            href="http://www.hercenter.org/"
            class="usa-link usa-link--external"
            >Bookmark Healthcare Environmental Resource Center</a
          >
          <p class="margin-top-0">
            This site provides pollution prevention and compliance assistance
            information for the healthcare sector. It is intended to be a
            comprehensive resource, covering all the varieties of hospital
            wastes, and all the rules that apply to them.
          </p>
        </li>
        <hr />
        <li>
          <a href="https://lgean.net/" class="usa-link usa-link--external"
            >Bookmark Local Government Environmental Assistance Network (LGEAN)</a
          >
          <p class="margin-top-0">
            The Local Government Environmental Assistance Network (LGEAN) is a
            "first-stop shop" providing environmental management, planning,
            funding, and regulatory information for local government elected and
            appointed officials, managers and staff.
          </p>
        </li>
        <hr />
        <li>
          <a
            href="http://www.ccar-greenlink.org/"
            class="usa-link usa-link--external"
            >Bookmark National Automotive Environmental Compliance Assistance
            Center (CCAR-Greenlink)</a
          >
          <p class="margin-top-0">
            CCAR-GreenLink®, is the National Automotive Environmental Compliance
            Assistance Center for the automotive industry. It is operated by the
            Coordinating Committee For Automotive Repair in cooperation with the
            U.S. Environmental Protection Agency. All documents are created by
            Federal and State EPA and OSHA offices, as well as the automotive
            industry.
          </p>
        </li>
        <hr />
        <li>
          <a
            href="https://www.ideals.illinois.edu/handle/2142/104621"
            class="usa-link usa-link--external"
            >Bookmark Printers' National Environmental Assistance Center (PNEAC)</a
          >
          <p class="margin-top-0">
            PNEAC is the first and only national collaborative of industry,
            university, state and federal organizations working to help the
            printing industry work cleaner, more efficiently and to stay ahead
            of the environmental compliance curve.
          </p>
        </li>
        <hr />
        <li>
          <a href="http://www.nmfrc.org/" class="usa-link usa-link--external"
            >Bookmark Surface Technology Environmental Resource Center (STERC)</a
          >
          <p class="margin-top-0">
            STERC, previously known as the National Metal Finishing Resource
            Center (NMFRC), provides environmental compliance information to the
            surface finishing and surface treatment industry. STERC is the
            result of a new partnership with NCMS, the AESF Foundation and NASF
            initiated in 2016 and through continued grant funding from EPA.
          </p>
        </li>
        <hr />
      </div>
    </div>
  </PageWithSideBarNav>
</RootLayout>
